In this practical was to estimate the token usage and cost of an LLM-based feature before using it in an application. It also checks whether the expected traffic fits within the configured rate limits and budget.
Created a FeatureBudget data class. It reads the usage assumptions and limits from environment variables, such as requests per day, average input and output tokens, peak requests per minute, token prices, RPM limit, TPM limit and daily/monthly budgets.

The calculate() method works out the expected input tokens, output tokens, total tokens per day, daily cost and monthly cost. It also adds a safety margin to the peak request and token estimates. Finally, it checks the estimates against the configured limits and prints PASS or REVIEW.

 Files used

- budget.py – contains the budget calculation and report.
- test_budget.py – checks the calculations and limit checks.
- requirements.txt – contains python-dotenv.
- .env – contains the assumptions and limits used by the program. Keep personal configuration files private.

pip install -r requirements.txt
.env
- REQUESTS_PER_DAY
- AVG_INPUT_TOKENS
- AVG_OUTPUT_TOKENS
- PEAK_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE
- INPUT_PRICE_PER_MILLION
- OUTPUT_PRICE_PER_MILLION
- RPM_LIMIT
- TPM_LIMIT
- MONTHLY_BUDGET_USD
- DAILY_BUDGET_USD
- SAFETY_MARGIN_PERCENT


python budget.py
python -m unittest test_budget.py

Output / observation

The program prints the estimated token usage and cost, peak RPM and TPM after applying the safety margin, and the result of each budget and capacity check. It gives an overall recommendation based on those checks.


